Three MAJOR issues from the review of #370:

MAJOR-1 (provenance fencing): the SessionStart digest and the orientation MEMORY
section injected RAW note.note / issue.title into agent context — bypassing the
fence #369 added to `forge recall`. Now both wrap content via fenceUntrusted()
(source 'memory' for notes, 'issue-titles' for issues), applied AFTER applyBudget
truncation so the ⟦END UNTRUSTED⟧ close marker always survives. A planted note/
title is DATA, not instructions.

MAJOR-2 (--limit ignored → claimed vanishes): `issue ready --json --limit N`
returns the whole set, so the digest dumped all ready issues and applyBudget
truncated CLAIMED (the tail) away. defaultFetchIssues now hard-caps with
.slice(0, limit) (CLI limit untrusted), and issuesSection orders CLAIMED before
ready so the agent's in-progress work is never the truncated tail.

MAJOR-3 (bare `forge` in hook): rendered a bare `forge hooks session-start` — on a
hook's minimal PATH it silently no-ops, or a foreign `forge` (this env's global
misroutes to Beads) injects its stdout as context. Now renders a RESOLVED
`node "<abs bin/forge.js>"` invocation (via __dirname; works in-repo and under
node_modules).

Rebased onto #369 to consume lib/untrusted-content.js. Filed follow-ups:
4a860df0 (path-keyed worktree dedup), 8e38896c (session-start stderr noise).

